okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Every session-backup operation in the menu (targets add/select/test/remove, list, verify, restore, prune, backup key, numeric options) and the incremental backup visible in the UI."
reported: "User, 2026-10-09/10: '메뉴에서 타겟 추가하고 선택할 수 있게 해줘. 원칙위반. UI에 반영이되지않은것은 개발 종료로 보지않아 … 심각한 규정위반', then '세션 백업에 증분백업도 지원해야하', then '나이트리 패치 , 로컬배포'. Rule saved to memory (ui-exposure-is-done)."
changes:
  menu: "session_backup_menu.py rewritten: rows 'Back up this session now [incremental · last …]', 'Snapshots of this folder', 'Restore a snapshot…' (snapshot, optional other folder, files yes/no, explicit yes), 'Verify a snapshot…', 'Prune old snapshots now', one row per target '[x] name [type · place]' (Enter: use on/off · test · remove; the built-in local can be deselected but not removed; at least one stays selected), 'Add a target…' (local / ssh / s3 / rclone fields, validation, write-read-delete test, select), schedule toggles, interval, minimum minutes between turn backups, keep last/daily, 'Backup key for credentials' (key file; a new random 64-hex key is created when missing). Main row 18 shows 'incremental · schedule · to <targets> · last …'."
  incremental: "Snapshots were already incremental (content-addressed chunks, only missing chunks uploaded); now shown: backup result 'incremental: N of M chunks new, X MB uploaded (snapshot Y MB)', snapshot list '+X MB new (N/M chunks)' per snapshot (from manifest stats), CLI list 'new=… (N/M chunks)' and create 'incremental: …'."
  key_file: "settings key_file is used by every backup/restore (CLI, menu, automatic triggers) when --key-file is not given; the key file is never collected even if it sits in the work folder (CollectOptions.skip_paths)."
  prelaunch: "panel prompts through prompt_menu_value (line mode), separator rows ignored."
tests: "tests/test_session_backup.py +5 (menu add/test/select/remove target, plain S3 secret rejected, key file + numbers, restore flow with confirmation, key file never collected). Groups: unit 1796 OK, runtime 398 OK, router 1175 OK; channel: test_channel_transcript_repository BoundaryScanDeadlineTests (2 tests) fail intermittently - also on committed HEAD e7f4169 in a separate worktree (1 of 3 runs), so not from this change; cause not investigated. ruff clean; ciel_runtime.py 4980 lines; router 9611 200."
e2e:
  harness: "evidence/e2e_menu_targets.py + e2e_menu_steps.py + console_driver.py: the menu runs in its own conhost window (e2e-3 scratch layout); a detached driver attaches to that console, writes real key events (WriteConsoleInputW) and reads the screen (ReadConsoleOutputCharacterW), waiting for each prompt. Screen text and a window capture are saved per step (e2e-5-menu-targets/shots)."
  result: "Run 2026-10-09 23:53: every step passed - target nas added through the menu with its test ('write, read and delete worked'), local deselected, nas tested from its row, key file created (64 hex), two backups (first +0.4 MB new 85/87 chunks, second 'incremental: 1 of 87 chunks new, 0.0 MB uploaded (snapshot 4.4 MB)'), list on nas, verify 'complete, every chunk checks out', restore 'Restored 88 files …; credentials restored' with a safety snapshot, prune 'removed 0, kept 3'. Settings file then: targets {nas}, default_targets [nas], key_file set. The key was not in any nas chunk."
incidents:
  - "Earlier SendKeys-based attempts were unreliable (keys before the menu was ready, IME, clipboard timing). In one attempt Enter landed on '9. Launch' and the pasted words 'local'/'nas' were sent by Codex through the router to the real ChatGPT Codex endpoint with the scratch test API key; it answered 401 Unauthorized. Later attempts set the routed upstream to a closed local port, and the final harness no longer uses SendKeys."
  - "The first console-driver run showed the key message cut off by a long path; the menu now puts 'New random backup key created.' on its own first line."
not_verified:
  - "SSH/S3/rclone targets added through the menu (the menu path is the same build_target + probe as the CLI targets verified in e2e-2; this menu run used a local-folder target)."
